    "summary": "Compressed request bodies can exhaust memory before extractor limits apply",
    "details": "Body extractors do not pass their size limits to the decompression layer.\nA small compressed request can therefore cause a large allocation before the\nextractor rejects the decoded body. A remote attacker can use this to exhaust\nmemory or CPU resources and cause denial of service.\n\nThis affects applications that read compressed request bodies with the\ncorresponding compression feature enabled.\n\nUpgrade to actix-web 4.18.2 or later with actix-http 3.20.1 or later.\nAs a workaround, reject compressed request bodies at a reverse proxy or in\nmiddleware before body extraction.",
